WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.920
NBC's smash hit sitcom The Office captivated&nbsp;
audiences as it unfolded in a nine-season run&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:11.040
from 2005 to 2013. And now, we’re breaking&nbsp;
down exactly what happened during the show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:13.920
so let’s dig deep into the&nbsp;
entire story of The Office.

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:19.280
Let's kick things off at the beginning, shall&nbsp;
we? The story of The Office begins in 2005,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:22.720
when a film crew from PBS arrives at the&nbsp;
Scranton branch of the Dunder Mifflin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:26.800
paper company to make a documentary about the&nbsp;
shifting landscape of American office life.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:30.560
There they meet Michael Scott, a former paper&nbsp;
salesman who's risen through the ranks to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:34.640
become the regional manager of the branch, and&nbsp;
the various characters who populate his staff.

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:38.720
Though the documentary crew perhaps didn't intend&nbsp;
to stay long, they are quickly sucked into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:43.440
various shenanigans around the office, including&nbsp;
the wild ideas of top salesman Dwight Schrute and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:47.760
the obvious flirtation between salesman Jim&nbsp;
Halpert and receptionist Pam Beesly. At the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:51.760
beginning of their tenure, the crew documents&nbsp;
the hiring of new temp worker Ryan Howard,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:55.120
and perhaps sensing that there's much&nbsp;
more drama to mine, they end up staying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:59.520
at Dunder Mifflin Scranton through major change&nbsp;
after major change for the next nine years.

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:04.720
Rumors soon begin to swirl throughout the company&nbsp;
that downsizing may be coming in the near future.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:07.760
Health care plans are slashed, and&nbsp;
Michael lets employee Devon White&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:11.200
go on Halloween through a bungled,&nbsp;
painful display of incompetence.

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:14.240
In spite of this, Michael tries his&nbsp;
best to increase company morale through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:17.840
less-than-successful means, which include&nbsp;
a haphazard basketball game between the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:21.840
office and warehouse workers, an impromptu&nbsp;
birthday party for alcoholic Meredith Palmer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:25.840
and a botched Christmas gift exchange. Perhaps&nbsp;
the best boost for the employees' attitudes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:28.560
comes in the form of an undercover&nbsp;
reading of Michael's screenplay,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:32.320
Threat Level Midnight, along with a&nbsp;
healthy dose of office-based Olympics.

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:36.240
Around this time, Michael buys a condo&nbsp;
and begins juggling a complicated pair of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:41.040
relationships with his realtor, Carol Stills,&nbsp;
and his superior, Jan Levinson. Meanwhile,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:44.560
beet-loving salesman Dwight Schrute and&nbsp;
uptight accountant Angela Martin begin a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:49.280
secret relationship, and by January 2006,&nbsp;
Jim breaks up with his girlfriend, Katy.

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:53.440
Not long after this, Michael reveals to corporate&nbsp;
that he's been in a "relationship" with Jan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:57.280
although he manages to explain that it&nbsp;
wasn't serious enough to warrant termination.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:01.200
And as spring turns to summer, Jim finally&nbsp;
expresses his feelings to Pam and kisses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:05.040
her. However, she stays with her fiancé,&nbsp;
warehouse worker Roy Anderson — although&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:09.760
they break up soon afterward — and Jim takes a&nbsp;
job at the Stamford branch of Dunder Mifflin.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:12.800
Back in the Scranton office, Ryan&nbsp;
the temp finally goes full time.

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:18.560
Michael kicks off the fall of 2006 by outing&nbsp;
and then kissing gay accountant Oscar Martinez,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:21.120
who gets a three-month paid vacation as a result.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:24.880
The manager follows this up by dramatically&nbsp;
shepherding the office through grief counseling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:28.480
after receiving news of the unexpected&nbsp;
death of former manager Ed Truck.

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:32.080
This all leads to a crescendo late in&nbsp;
the year when Jan informs Michael that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:35.600
the Scranton branch is being closed.&nbsp;
However, when the Stamford manager,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:40.400
Josh Porter, ditches his managerial duties for&nbsp;
a job with Staples, the script is flipped, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:44.960
Scranton ends up absorbing the Stamford branch,&nbsp;
bringing Jim back to Pennsylvania in the process.

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:46.791
"We did it!"

00:02:46.791 --> 00:02:49.446
"We did it!"

00:02:49.446 --> 00:02:54.480
The merger of the two branches is a rough one, and&nbsp;
by early 2007, Andy Bernard and Karen Filippelli,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:59.200
who also happens to be Jim's new girlfriend, are&nbsp;
the only original Stamford employees remaining.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:03.600
Later, Pam's ex-fiance Roy is fired when he&nbsp;
tries to assault Jim after learning that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:09.120
kissed Pam. Dwight is also framed by Andy and&nbsp;
fired, although he's quickly rehired afterward.

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:12.800
This period of time also sees a lot of&nbsp;
drama in the relationship department.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:16.880
Carol breaks up with Michael, who steers&nbsp;
into the relationship with Jan as a result.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:20.000
Salesman Phyllis Lapin [LAP-in] also&nbsp;
ties the knot with Bob Vance of Vance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:24.000
Refrigeration and heads off on a six-week&nbsp;
honeymoon. Soon after the wedding, Michael&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:28.400
interviews with CFO David Wallace to replace&nbsp;
Jan at the corporate office, but ultimately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:32.400
that job goes to Ryan Howard, who becomes&nbsp;
the youngest VP in the company's history.

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:37.040
In the aftermath of Ryan Howard's promotion,&nbsp;
Jim breaks up with Karen and finally hooks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:41.520
up with Pam. Angela privately breaks up&nbsp;
with Dwight after he mercy-kills her cat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:46.160
and she begins dating Andy openly. Michael&nbsp;
continues to date Jan, who helps him organize&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:51.040
a charity "Fun Run" to raise funds for rabies&nbsp;
awareness after he hits Meredith with his car.

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:53.440
Yes, those two events are connected.

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:58.160
"Turns out Meredith has been exposed to rabies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:02.560
which is like 10 times worse than&nbsp;
a little crack in your pelvis."

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:06.960
Meanwhile, looking to make a splash, Ryan&nbsp;
attempts to launch a company website called&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:11.680
"Dunder Mifflin Infinity." The site goes&nbsp;
live in October 2007, but six months later,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:15.680
it's dead in the water, and Ryan has been&nbsp;
arrested for misleading the shareholders.

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:21.040
As Dunder Mifflin struggles, Jan sues the company,&nbsp;
unsuccessfully, for wrongful termination. She also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:24.880
bankrupts Michael, and then the two break up&nbsp;
after throwing the world's worst dinner party.

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:27.840
"Oh good, I'll be your first customer."

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:29.200
"You're hardly my first."

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:31.520
"That's what she said!"

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:36.240
Throughout the chaos, Jim and Pam's fledgling&nbsp;
relationship soars. Jim attempts to propose to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:41.520
Pam in early 2008, but Andy steals his thunder by&nbsp;
proposing to Angela first at the farewell party&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:47.520
for Toby Flenderson — the HR rep who's leaving for&nbsp;
Costa Rica. Toby is replaced by Holly Flax, who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:51.440
immediately hits things off with Michael, because&nbsp;
the two are just so perfectly dorky together.

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:56.240
The rest of 2008 is fairly quiet&nbsp;
as far as the office is concerned.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.240 --> 00:05:00.000
The biggest events are the return of Ryan&nbsp;
Howard as a temp and the transfer of Holly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:04.160
Flax to the Nashua branch after David Wallace&nbsp;
discovers that she and Michael are dating.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:08.160
This effectively breaks the couple up, although&nbsp;
the two are still interested in each other.

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:12.080
Jim and Pam's relationship also comes under&nbsp;
serious pressure for the first time when Pam&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:16.560
leaves for three months to attend art school in&nbsp;
New York City. Jim proposes to her while she's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:21.280
away, and eventually, she returns after failing&nbsp;
to complete the course. Not long after this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:25.760
Jim buys his parents' house without telling&nbsp;
Pam and then surprises her with it as a gift.

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:30.560
As the year wraps up, things take a major turn.&nbsp;
Despite the fact that she's engaged to Andy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:32.640
Angela has been having an affair with Dwight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:36.720
but that all comes crashing down when&nbsp;
Phyllis exposes Angela's infidelity.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:41.280
And early in 2009, the two salesmen duel&nbsp;
with each other over their coworker. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:45.280
by the time it's over, both combatants have&nbsp;
decided to bitterly break things off with Angela.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:50.000
In early 2009, Michael and Pam go on&nbsp;
a Dunder Mifflin lecture circuit where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:54.880
Michael reveals his masterfully dramatic recipe&nbsp;
for success to everyone who will listen to him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.880 --> 00:05:59.680
Afterward, David Wallace hires Charles Miner&nbsp;
to fill Ryan's old job. Charles immediately&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:03.600
clashes with Michael, who quits after one&nbsp;
day of working with the new supervisor.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:07.520
Having little experience outside of the paper&nbsp;
market, Michael decides to start his own paper&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.520 --> 00:06:12.160
company and convinces Pam and Ryan to join&nbsp;
him. After a short run of artificial success,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:16.720
the trio uses the Michael Scott Paper Company&nbsp;
as leverage to get jobs back at Dunder Mifflin.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:20.720
Pam is promoted to sales, while Erin&nbsp;
Hannon stays on as the new receptionist.

00:06:20.720 --> 00:06:24.880
After this, Pam and Jim discover they're going to&nbsp;
have a kid as they tend to an injury Pam received&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:28.720
at a company picnic. They manage to keep the&nbsp;
pregnancy a secret until the fall when the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:33.520
rumor-mill accidentally leaks the information. In&nbsp;
the interim, Dunder Mifflin closes their Buffalo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.520 --> 00:06:37.360
Camden, and Yonkers branches, and it's clear&nbsp;
the company is on the way to bankruptcy.

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:42.400
In the fall of 2009, Jim and Michael are made&nbsp;
co-managers in order to spread out the increased&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:46.720
workload caused by all of the branch closings.&nbsp;
The dynamic duo lead the office through the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.720 --> 00:06:51.280
ensuing months, during which Dunder Mifflin goes&nbsp;
under and is bought by the printer company Sabre.

00:06:51.280 --> 00:06:55.280
As Dunder Mifflin tanks, Jim and Pam's&nbsp;
relationship reaches new heights as they get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.280 --> 00:06:59.760
hitched in Niagara Falls, a deliberately-planned&nbsp;
destination wedding they hope their coworkers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:03.920
will skip. But despite the distance, the&nbsp;
entire office tags along for the ride.

00:07:03.920 --> 00:07:08.800
Once Sabre CEO Jo Bennett and her lackey, Gabe&nbsp;
Lewis, arrive on the scene, Jim quickly returns&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.800 --> 00:07:13.440
to sales, and Michael resumes sole command on&nbsp;
the Dunder Mifflin managerial throne. The affable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:17.600
Darryl Philbin is promoted during this time as&nbsp;
well, and he begins to fulfill his duties from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:23.200
office rather than the warehouse. In March 2010, a&nbsp;
very pregnant Pam spends an entire fearful day at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:27.520
the office before being talked into going to the&nbsp;
hospital where she gives birth to Cecelia Halpert.

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:31.200
With the heavy days of perpetual&nbsp;
downsizing behind them for the time being,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:34.080
the Scranton office enters a&nbsp;
period of relative stability.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:38.960
Toby returns from Costa Rica and Pam, who's&nbsp;
miserable in sales, creates the position of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.960 --> 00:07:42.880
"office administrator" out of thin air, and&nbsp;
then awards it to herself as a promotion.

00:07:42.880 --> 00:07:47.760
As 2010 draws to a close, Toby spends a chunk&nbsp;
of time out of the office serving as a juror on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:52.080
the case of the Scranton Strangler. This leads&nbsp;
to Holly temporarily returning as a fill-in,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.080 --> 00:07:55.360
giving Michael the chance to convince&nbsp;
her to date him once again, and soon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.360 --> 00:08:00.720
the two love birds are back together. Early 2011&nbsp;
sees the over-the-top romantic couple get engaged&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.720 --> 00:08:04.880
and then move away together to Boulder, Colorado,&nbsp;
where they plan to help Holly's aging parents.

00:08:05.920 --> 00:08:07.840
"Hey, will you guys let me&nbsp;
know if this ever airs?"

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:09.120
The departure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:13.440
of Michael Scott leaves the office scrambling,&nbsp;
yet again, to fill the void. Initially, Michael&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:18.320
trains Deangelo Vickers to replace him. However,&nbsp;
soon after taking the job, Deangelo is seriously&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.320 --> 00:08:22.400
injured while performing a basketball stunt,&nbsp;
and the office finds itself leaderless again.

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:27.280
Sabre CEO Jo Bennet swoops in to the rescue and&nbsp;
offers Dwight the position of acting manager for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:31.600
the time being. But Dwight finds himself relegated&nbsp;
back to the bullpen after accidentally firing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.600 --> 00:08:35.920
a loaded gun in the office. Jo then sets up a&nbsp;
search committee, which finally settles on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.920 --> 00:08:39.920
uncomfortably eccentric Robert California&nbsp;
as the new regional manager. He promptly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.920 --> 00:08:44.480
convinces Jo Bennet to give him her own job&nbsp;
and then hires Andy Bernard as his replacement.

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:49.360
As 2011 plays out, Robert California&nbsp;
plays mind games with his new staff and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.360 --> 00:08:53.200
puts unreasonable pressure on Andy&nbsp;
to push the office to overperform.

00:08:53.200 --> 00:08:56.880
Andy, on the other hand, takes some time to&nbsp;
acclimate to his new position of authority,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.880 --> 00:09:00.240
initially struggling to handle crises&nbsp;
— like the warehouse workers winning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.240 --> 00:09:04.880
the lottery and all quitting at once. He also&nbsp;
begins dating Jessica, one of the few repeat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.880 --> 00:09:08.560
characters in the show that actually works&nbsp;
outside of the office and the greater story.

00:09:08.560 --> 00:09:12.720
In the meantime, Cathy Simms is hired as a&nbsp;
temp to replace Pam while she's on maternity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.720 --> 00:09:16.240
leave with her second child, Philip.&nbsp;
Angela gives birth to her first child,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:20.480
who's also named Philip and who she claims to&nbsp;
have had with her husband, Senator Robert Lipton,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.480 --> 00:09:25.600
yet another extracurricular character from outside&nbsp;
the office who met Angela back in late 2010.

00:09:26.320 --> 00:09:31.280
In early 2012, Dwight leads a team from Dunder&nbsp;
Mifflin Scranton down to Tallahassee, Florida,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.280 --> 00:09:35.440
where they work in the Sabre headquarters for&nbsp;
three weeks on a project led by Nellie Bertram.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.440 --> 00:09:39.280
The group is tasked with designing a new&nbsp;
retail store for the printer company. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.280 --> 00:09:43.520
the entire situation goes south when Robert&nbsp;
California deliberately nixes the idea,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:46.240
and soon everyone finds&nbsp;
themselves back in Scranton.

00:09:46.240 --> 00:09:48.480
It's during this time that Andy ditches Jessica,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:53.360
heads to Florida to fetch ex-girlfriend Erin, and&nbsp;
reignites a relationship with the receptionist.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:57.280
However, when the couple returns to Scranton,&nbsp;
Andy finds he's been usurped by Nellie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.280 --> 00:10:01.920
who's taken the manager position on the grounds&nbsp;
that Andy had abandoned his responsibilities.

00:10:01.920 --> 00:10:05.440
Not long after this, Jo Bennet&nbsp;
liquidates the entire Sabre company,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.440 --> 00:10:08.800
just in time for David Wallace to&nbsp;
return to the scene as a new investor.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.800 --> 00:10:12.960
He reinstates Andy as the manager, while&nbsp;
Nellie is allowed to stay on as an employee.

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:15.920
In late 2012, Andy receives news that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:20.080
his family has gone bankrupt, which leads to him&nbsp;
taking an undisclosed three-month break so that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.080 --> 00:10:25.200
he can sail the family yacht to the Caribbean in&nbsp;
order to sell it. Upon his return, a justifiably&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:29.600
angry Erin breaks up with him and starts dating&nbsp;
the new customer service rep, Pete Miller.

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:34.000
While all that drama is happening, Jim starts&nbsp;
to work part-time after going "all in" on his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:39.360
own sports marketing company in Philly, a business&nbsp;
called Athlead. This new focus quickly escalates,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:44.480
and by early 2013, Jim and Pam's relationship&nbsp;
is under serious strain. They begin attending&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.480 --> 00:10:48.240
marital counseling, and eventually, Jim&nbsp;
realizes that he can't continue dividing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:48.240 --> 00:10:53.200
his time between Philly and Scranton. He returns&nbsp;
to Dunder Mifflin full-time late in the spring.

00:10:53.200 --> 00:10:57.520
This all coincides with Andy Bernard's third and&nbsp;
final abrupt departure from the company when he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.520 --> 00:11:02.240
quits in order to pursue an acting career.&nbsp;
In his wake, Dwight at long last is truly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.240 --> 00:11:06.240
unquestionably crowned as the regional&nbsp;
manager of Dunder Mifflin Scranton.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.240 --> 00:11:10.160
Plus, it finally comes out that Angela's&nbsp;
son isn't the senator's but Dwight's.

00:11:10.960 --> 00:11:16.240
In May 2013, PBS airs the documentary that's&nbsp;
been "ten years in the making." The Scranton&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.240 --> 00:11:20.720
office is officially no longer being watched&nbsp;
by a documentary crew around the clock. Over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:20.720 --> 00:11:25.440
the following year, new regional manager Dwight&nbsp;
Schrute makes several changes, including rehiring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:25.440 --> 00:11:30.560
Devon and firing accountant Kevin Malone, who&nbsp;
buys his own bar. Plus, salesman Stanley Hudson&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:30.560 --> 00:11:35.360
finally retires to a hideaway in Florida, where he&nbsp;
spends his time alone, carving wooden figurines.

00:11:35.920 --> 00:11:39.920
A year after the documentary airs, the film&nbsp;
crew catches up with everyone in order to gather&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:39.920 --> 00:11:44.560
bonus footage for the DVD release. Dwight and&nbsp;
Angela are officially married during this time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:44.560 --> 00:11:49.040
and Michael Scott arrives as a surprise guest at&nbsp;
the wedding, revealing that he's very happy living&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:49.040 --> 00:11:53.440
his life with Holly and their kids in Colorado.&nbsp;
We also learn that Pam has been plotting to sell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:53.440 --> 00:11:58.240
the Halpert house and move her family to Austin,&nbsp;
Texas, so Jim can resume his career with Athlead.

00:11:58.240 --> 00:12:02.320
With everyone's lives officially moving forward,&nbsp;
many in directions other than the office,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:02.320 --> 00:12:05.680
the epic tale of America's favorite&nbsp;
workplace finally comes to an end.

